This is a finite independent review of the work-only Notes notebook-confirmation cancellation correction. Production was not changed.

The fresh run passed 22/22 checks with no skips: the earlier review's 16 test bodies were retained, with three runtime import-path replacements, and six fresh checks covered real synthetic attachment bytes, Cancel and Escape, a trashed note, failed persistence followed by explicit retry, an already pending attachment request, and a clean pending Save. Cancel sent no additional request, retained attachment/editor element identities and focus/inert state, and allowed the pending Save to advance the revision before a subsequent draft save.

Tests use a bounded DOM element model and the candidate's actual Notes handlers. Five attachment fixtures wrote/read owned temporary files and removed their confined directories. There was no browser, original application, original GUI, benchmark, production host, or external account execution in this review. These checks do not establish full accessibility or browser acceptance.

The exact two source substitutions reconstruct client 90886819feef847847fcae8c442e0a401a1146a7a4aa1fd862a54b5e01f41da9 from the prior client. Five backend/support modules remain identical. The strict 229-file candidate, prior 214-file author stage, and earlier 74-file review inventories authenticate before and after. Their manifests and prior failures remain unchanged.

The earlier author run remains separate: 69/69 source-stable, following its retained negative Cancel result and a 59/69 run missing 31 inert helper prerequisites. This review audited its retained observations and authenticated 13 exact released source spans, the conflict-ID helper, and four license records without re-executing original code. The audit records 41 selected top-level helper calls: 20 nesting, four path, four move, seven trash/restore mutation and six display calls. Two move smoke calls are separate from two candidate move projection comparisons. Seventy-three trash item projections compare five fields (365 field assertions); they are not whole-object comparisons. Eleven oracle constructions create 17 VM contexts with in-memory, fixed-clock and bounded SQL/model adapters. Recursive/internal helper invocation counts are not observed. Full Joplin database, synchronization, plugins and UI are outside this proof.

One source-only audit collector attempt failed because organization bindings have paths but no URLs. Its exact source and displayed output are preserved; no application failure is inferred. The passing 22-case run retains its exact collector source snapshots. The later strict inventory guard in prepare.mjs was authenticated by source-only checks; its added guard is not silently substituted into that historical run.

Paths in adapters.json identify only runtime import replacements. NOTES_REVIEW_OUTPUT directs all test observations to this review's own run directory. No test writes to app results or any frozen stage. review-validation.json binds the finite result; review-manifest.json gives the strict owned inventory. Complete product parity, original-grade security and superiority remain false.
